One vertex of the jittered sphere, half a local edge along its shape gradient (the vertex whose gradient has the largest normal part): the raw step (red) is 88 % normal. `constrain_direction` removes that part with the sphere's own normal and keeps the tangential step (blue); `snap` then removes the remaining distance to the sphere, 0.003 local edges here.
